# Story 37: Hop Command (45s)
# Hook: Transfer your AI context to another pane -- hop and resume seamlessly.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-37-hop-command.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 10

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- context follows you across panes.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
Build up some context in this pane.

[00:08.0 --> 00:11.0]
Run a few commands -- the AI remembers all of this.

[00:11.0 --> 00:14.0]
The conversation and shell history form a rich context.

[00:14.0 --> 00:20.0]
Split right and name the new pane 'target'.

[00:20.0 --> 00:24.0]
Go back to the original pane where your context lives.

[00:24.0 --> 00:30.0]
##hop target copies the full AI context to the target pane. Conversation history, tool results, everything transfers.

[00:30.0 --> 00:34.0]
Switch to the target pane to pick up where you left off.

[00:34.0 --> 00:40.0]
##hop resume tells the AI to continue with the transferred context -- no re-explaining needed.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Hop -- move your AI brain between panes instantly.

